rt raters, including the Cook Political Report and Sabato's Crystal Ball, call the race Lean D, while the Silver Bulletin rates it Likely D.\n\nBenson has raised about $12.5 million to James's $6.4 million and holds a large cash advantage heading into the final weeks. James remains a well-known Republican in an even-partisanship state, and the two Republican-sponsored polls show a closer contest than the nonpartisan surveys. Obama is scheduled to campaign with Benson in Detroit during debate week. The race leans clearly toward Benson but is not out of reach for James.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.912, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8925, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9071, "margin": 7.0}]}